{
  "name": "object-literal-to-unimplemented-callee",
  "description": "An object literal passed to a call or a new expression whose callee has no implementation in the target reads each member of the parameter type it is checked against, as the call instantiates it, through each constituent of a union or an intersection and through a nested literal: a construct signature or a type-literal method read off a global, a method of a declared global, a function a declaration file declares, a dependency's generic and the methods of the compiler's library. Where a function, an override, an overload implementation, an arrow or an object of the target stands for the callee, the literal reads nothing, so a member that callee never reads stays reported, even beside an implementation the target cannot see.",
  "languages": [
    "ts"
  ],
  "target_kind": "application",
